---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, CLARITY_ID, CONTACT_EMAIL, GA4_ID, LAST_UPDATED, LEGAL, SITE_NAMES, SITE_URL } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Legal notice of ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: publisher, host, liability`} description="Legal notice of Pension Estate Tax: the publisher Radif Partners, the host, what the UK inheritance tax and pension estimates cover, liability and reuse of public data." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Legal notice' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Legal notice</h1>
    <p>Information given under Article 6 III-1 of French law no. 2004-575 of 21 June 2004, the publisher being established in France.</p>
    <h2>Publisher</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <p>Publication director: {AUTHOR_NAME}, responsible for the content of {SITE_URL}.</p>
    <h2>Hosting provider</h2>
    <LegalIdentity mode="hosting" lang={lang} />
    <h2>What the site does</h2>
    <p>The site estimates the United Kingdom inheritance tax on an estate, including unused pension funds and pension death benefits for deaths on or after 6 April 2027 under the Finance Act 2026, and the income tax paid by beneficiaries on inherited pensions. It has no connection with HM Revenue and Customs, HM Treasury, any pension scheme, insurer, solicitor or financial adviser.</p>
    <h2>General information, not advice</h2>
    <p>The figures are estimates built on the assumptions set out on the <a href={route('method', lang)}>method page</a>. They are not tax, legal or financial advice and they are not a regulated personal recommendation. The tax actually due is the one established by the personal representatives of an estate on the inheritance tax account and agreed with HMRC; a decision about a will, a gift, a pension nomination or a withdrawal should be checked with a solicitor or a regulated financial adviser.</p>
    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>Each rule is taken from the legislation or HMRC page cited with it, and the calculation engine is tested before each build. The publisher gives no guarantee that no error or later change in the law remains and cannot be held liable for any decision taken on the basis of this site alone. Errors can be reported through the <a href={route('contact', lang)}>contact</a> page.</p>
    <h2>Intellectual property and reuse</h2>
    <p>Texts, graphics and code belong to the publisher. Legislation from legislation.gov.uk and guidance from GOV.UK are public sector information reused under the <a href="https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Open Government Licence v3.0</a>, with the source named on each page.</p>
    {/* gen-legal-pages:terms */}
    <h2>Personal data and cookies</h2>
    {GA4_ID ? (<p>What you type in the calculators stays in your browser. The site sets Google Analytics audience measurement cookies (<code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_{GA4_ID.replace('G-', '')}</code>, 13 months at most), with no advertising{CLARITY_ID && '; page stability is monitored with Microsoft Clarity, cookie-free'}. Details, legal basis and how to object: <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a> and <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies</a> page.</p>) : (<p>What you type in the calculators stays in your browser and the site sets no cookies{CLARITY_ID && '; page stability is monitored anonymously with Microsoft Clarity, cookie-free'}. See the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a> and the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies</a> page.</p>)}
    {/* /gen-legal-pages:terms */}
    <h2>Reporting unlawful content</h2><p><a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, with the page address and the reason.</p>
    <h2>Governing law</h2><p>French law. Failing an amicable solution, the courts of {LEGAL.jurisdiction} have jurisdiction, without prejudice to the mandatory rules protecting consumers in their country of residence. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
